╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [BUG] GeminiModel does not convert Vertex AI 429 with plain-text error message to ModelThrottledException                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ## Checks                                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ -  I have updated to the lastest minor and patch version of Strands                                                                             │
│ -  I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior                                                                           │
│ -  I have searched ./issues and there are no duplicates of my issue                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## SDK Language                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Python                                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Strands Version                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 1.47.0 (first observed on 1.45.0; the relevant code on `main` is unchanged)                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Language Runtime Version                                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Python 3.12                                                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Operating System                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ macOS 15 (Darwin 25.4.0)                                                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Installation Method                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ pip                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ When Vertex AI (`vertexai=True`) returns a 429 under concurrent load, the error arrives as a `genai.errors.ClientError` whose `message` is      │
│ **plain text**, not JSON:                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│ 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED. Resource exhausted. Please try again later. ...                                                                         │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ `GeminiModel.stream()` detects throttling by `json.loads(error.message)` and matching `message["error"]["status"]`. With a plain-text message,  │
│ `json.loads` raises `JSONDecodeError`, the handler logs a warning and re-raises the raw `ClientError` — so it is never converted to             │
│ `ModelThrottledException` and the event loop's built-in retry (`ModelRetryStrategy`) never fires.                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Deterministic reproduction (mirrors what the google-genai SDK raises mid-stream for a Vertex AI 429):                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ import asyncio                                                                                                                                  │
│ from unittest import mock                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ from google import genai                                                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ from strands.models.gemini import GeminiModel                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ # What Vertex AI's 429 looks like: structured code/status, plain-text message                                                                   │
│ error = genai.errors.ClientError(                                                                                                               │
│     429,                                                                                                                                        │
│     {"error": {"status": "RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED", "message": "Resource exhausted. Please try again later."}},                                      │
│ )                                                                                                                                               │
│ assert error.code == 429                                                                                                                        │
│ assert error.status == "RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED"                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ model = GeminiModel(model_id="gemini-2.5-flash", client_args={"api_key": "test"})                                                               │
│ with mock.patch.object(genai.Client, "aio", new_callable=mock.PropertyMock) as aio:                                                             │
│     aio.return_value.models.generate_content_stream.side_effect = error                                                                         │
│     events = model.stream([{"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "hi"}]}])                                                                      │
│     asyncio.run(events.__anext__())  # raises raw ClientError, not ModelThrottledException                                                      │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Real-world trigger: Vertex AI's pay-as-you-go Gemini models use Dynamic Shared Quota, so any concurrent traffic can receive a 429 regardless of │
│ configured quota. In my case, 1 out of 30 requests at concurrency 4 hit this (gemini model, `global` endpoint), and the error surfaced directly │
│ to the user instead of being retried.                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Expected Behavior                                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ A 429 (`RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`) from Vertex AI is converted to `ModelThrottledException`, regardless of whether `error.message` happens to be      │
│ JSON, so the built-in exponential-backoff retry in the event loop handles it.                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Actual Behavior                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The raw `genai.errors.ClientError` propagates out of `stream()`:                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│ strands  | error_message=<Resource exhausted. Please try again later. ...> | Gemini API returned non-JSON error                                 │
│ ...                                                                                                                                             │
│ google.genai.errors.ClientError: 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED. Resource exhausted. Please try again later. ...                                        │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ No retry is attempted; the request fails immediately.                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Additional Context                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - #1062 fixed the `JSONDecodeError` crash for non-JSON error messages (#1024), but the non-JSON path re-raises the raw `ClientError` without    │
│ ever checking for throttling — which is exactly the path a Vertex AI 429 takes.                                                                 │
│ - The SDK-level HTTP retry (`HttpRetryOptions`) does not help here: the 429 is raised while iterating the response stream                       │
│ (`errors.APIError.raise_error_async`), which is outside the request-issuing wrapper that `retry_options` covers.                                │
│ - The TypeScript SDK has the same root cause: `classifyGoogleError()` in `src/models/google/errors.ts` also relies on                           │
│ `JSON.parse(error.message)` and returns `undefined` for non-JSON messages, so a plain-text 429 is not classified as throttling there either.    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Possible Solution                                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ `genai.errors.APIError` already exposes structured `code` and `status` attributes (populated by the google-genai SDK from the response), so the │
│ handler doesn't need to parse `error.message` at all:                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ except genai.errors.ClientError as error:                                                                                                       │
│     match error.status:                                                                                                                         │
│         case "RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED" | "UNAVAILABLE":                                                                                              │
│             raise ModelThrottledException(error.message) from error                                                                             │
│         case "INVALID_ARGUMENT":                                                                                                                │
│             ...                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ I'd be happy to submit a PR for the Python SDK with this fix.                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Related Issues                                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ #1024, #1062, #370                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
